+# Silent Dialogue Universal 1.0.2 source audit
+
+This revision is an independent implementation based on the existing Silent Dialogue Universal source and public CommonLibSSE-NG interfaces. No source code from other silent-dialogue mods is included.
+
+## Voice-safety changes
+
+1. Voice resources are classified as present, missing, or unknown instead of using a simple true/false check.
+2. Existing exact resources are always preserved.
+3. Normal Skyrim voice paths are checked across the supported FUZ/XWM/WAV filename variants.
+4. Unknown/custom path formats are preserved rather than treated as missing.
+5. Dialogue responses with an explicit `voiceSound` descriptor are never replaced.
+6. The exact bundled `silence_N.fuz` resource is verified before modifying a response.
+7. Verbose logging records preservation decisions and actual substitutions.
+
+## Other observations
+
+- The subtitle force flag is only set when at least one response was actually substituted. It remains a runtime mutation of the associated topic-info form for the session; changing that behavior would require a separate subtitle-display hook and is intentionally not part of this safety revision.
+- Reading-time parsing and configuration bounds were reviewed; no blocking issue was found.
+- The constructor hook signature matches the CommonLibSSE-NG `DialogueItem` constructor wrapper used by this project.
